      "id": "act-25m",
      "title": "Twenty-five metres",
      "caption": "The block is not a shape. It is a distance.",
      "notes": "Sacchi allowed no more than 25 metres between the back line and the front two. Everything else in this system is a consequence of that one number: the pressing is possible because the distances are short, and the line can step because there is nobody stranded behind it.",
